SUMMARY:Adolf Ogi takes power (Switzerland)
DESCRIPTION:Adolf Ogi is a Swiss politician who most recently served as Spe
 cial Advisor to the UN Secretary General on Sport for Development and Peac
 e from 2001 to 2008. He previously served as member of the Federal Council
  (Switzerland) for the Swiss People's Party from 1987 to 2000. He held the
  Presidency of the Swiss Confederation twice in 1993 and 2000.\n\nNew lead
 er: Switzerland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Ogi\nText: Wi
 kipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:New leader
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Ogi
