SUMMARY:2000 Dominican general election
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Dominica on 31 January 2000 and 
 saw the Dominica Labour Party led by Rosie Douglas take power defeating th
 e previous government of the United Workers' Party led by Edison James\, d
 espite the UWP receiving more votes. The DLP won 10 seats\, the UWP 9 seat
 s and the Dominica Freedom Party took 2 seats. Voter turnout was 59.25%.\n
 \nElection: Dominica\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000_Dominican
 _general_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.de
 v).
