SUMMARY:Earthquake: 2001 Gujarat earthquake (India)
DESCRIPTION:An earthquake struck India and Pakistan on 26 January 2001 at 0
 8:46 am IST. The epicentre was about 9 km south-southwest of the village o
 f Chobari in Bhachau Taluka of Kutch district in Gujarat\, India. The eart
 hquake had a maximum Mercalli intensity of XII (Extreme).\n\nCrisis: India
 \nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2001_Gujarat_earthquake\nText: Wik
 ipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Crisis
