SUMMARY:Twenty-first Amendment of the Constitution of Ireland
DESCRIPTION:The Twenty-first Amendment of the Constitution Act 2001 is an a
 mendment of the Constitution of Ireland which introduced a constitutional 
 ban on the death penalty and removed all references to capital punishment 
 from the text. It was approved by referendum on 7 June 2001 and signed int
 o law on 27 March 2002.\n\nElection: Ireland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia
 .org/wiki/Twenty-first_Amendment_of_the_Constitution_of_Ireland\nText: Wik
