SUMMARY:Twenty-fourth Amendment of the Constitution Bill 2001 (Ireland)
DESCRIPTION:The Twenty-fourth Amendment of the Constitution Bill 2001 was a
  proposed amendment to the Constitution of Ireland to allow the state to r
 atify the Treaty of Nice of the European Union. The proposal was rejected 
 in a referendum held in June 2001\, sometimes referred to as the first Nic
 e referendum.\n\nElection: Ireland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/
