SUMMARY:2002 Slovenian presidential election
DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Slovenia in 2002. The first
  round was held on 10 November\, with a run-off held on 1 December after n
 o candidate passed the 50% threshold in the first round. The result was a 
 victory for Janez Drnovšek\, who won 56.6% of the vote in the second roun
 d. Voter turnout was 72.04% in the first round and 65.24% in the second.\n
 \nElection: Slovenia\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002_Slovenian
 _presidential_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pag
 es.dev).
