SUMMARY:2002–2003 Venezuelan general strike
DESCRIPTION:The Venezuelan general strike of 2002–2003 was an attempt by 
 the Venezuelan opposition to President Hugo Chávez to summon a new presid
 ential election. It took place from December 2002 to February 2003\, when 
 it faded. The government fired over 18\,000 PDVSA employees and arrest war
 rants were issued for the presidents of the striking organizations.\n\nPro
 test: Venezuela\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002%E2%80%932003_V
 enezuelan_general_strike\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.p
 ages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Protest
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002%E2%80%932003_Venezuelan_general_stri
 ke
