DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20030116
SUMMARY:Eldred v. Ashcroft (United States)
DESCRIPTION:Eldred v. Ashcroft\, 537 U.S. 186 (2003)\, was a decision by th
 e Supreme Court of the United States upholding the constitutionality of th
 e 1998 Sonny Bono Copyright Term Extension Act (CTEA). Plaintiffs\, led by
  Internet publisher Eric Eldred\, argued that the statute was unconstituti
 onal. The Supreme Court disagreed and allowed the statute to remain in eff
 ect.\n\nCourt ruling: United States\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki
 /Eldred_v._Ashcroft\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.
 dev).
CATEGORIES:Court ruling
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eldred_v._Ashcroft
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
