DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Finland on 16 March 2003. 
 The Centre Party led by Anneli Jäätteenmäki overtook the Social Democra
 tic Party (SDP) to become the largest party in the Eduskunta. This was cre
 dited mainly to Jäätteenmäki's powerful leadership and modernization of
  the party still often viewed as agrarian and conservative by many.\n\nEle
 ction: Finland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2003_Finnish_parliam
