DESCRIPTION:A general election was held in Spain on 14 March 2004 to elect 
 the members of the 8th Cortes Generales under the Spanish Constitution of 
 1978. All 350 seats in the Congress of Deputies were up for election\, as 
 well as 208 of 259 seats in the Senate. It was held concurrently with a re
 gional election in Andalusia.\n\nElection: Spain\nSource: https://en.wikip
 edia.org/wiki/2004_Spanish_general_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0
