SUMMARY:2004 Antiguan general election (Antigua and Barbuda)
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Antigua and Barbuda on 23 March 
 2004. The result was a victory for the opposition United Progressive Party
  (UPP)\, which defeated the incumbent Antigua Labour Party. Baldwin Spence
 r\, leader of the UPP\, replaced Lester Bird as Prime Minister of Antigua 
 and Barbuda\, with Bird being one of eight Labour MPs to lose his seat.\n\
 nElection: Antigua and Barbuda\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2004
