DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20070716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20070717
SUMMARY:Earthquake: 2007 Chūetsu offshore earthquake (Japan)
DESCRIPTION:A magnitude 6.6 earthquake occurred 10:13 local time on July 16
 \, 2007\, at a previously unknown offshore fault in the northwest Niigata 
 Prefecture of Japan. The city of Kashiwazaki and the villages of Iizuna an
 d Kariwa registered the highest seismic intensity of a strong 6 on Japan's
  shindo scale\, and the quake was felt as far away as Tokyo.\n\nCrisis: Ja
 pan\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_Ch%C5%ABetsu_offshore_eart
 hquake\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Crisis
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_Ch%C5%ABetsu_offshore_earthquake
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
