DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20070813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20070814
SUMMARY:Natural disaster: Hurricane Dean
DESCRIPTION:Hurricane Dean was the most powerful and destructive tropical c
 yclone of the 2007 Atlantic hurricane season. It ties with Hurricane Mitch
  for the tenth most intense Atlantic hurricane by atmospheric pressure. Ad
 ditionally\, it made the fifth most intense landfall in the basin by centr
 al pressure.\n\nCrisis: International\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wi
 ki/Hurricane_Dean\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.de
 v).
CATEGORIES:Crisis
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Dean
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
