DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20070815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20070816
SUMMARY:Earthquake: 2007 Peru earthquake
DESCRIPTION:The 2007 Peru earthquake\, which measured 8.0 on the moment mag
 nitude scale\, hit the central coast of Peru on August 15 at 23:40:57 UTC 
 and lasted two minutes. The epicenter was located 150 km (93 mi) south-sou
 theast of Lima at a depth of 39 km (24 mi). At least 595 people died and o
 ver 2\,290 people were injured.\n\nCrisis: Peru\nSource: https://en.wikipe
 dia.org/wiki/2007_Peru_earthquake\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PR
 P (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Crisis
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_Peru_earthquake
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
