SUMMARY:Terrorist attack: 2008 Mumbai attacks (India)
DESCRIPTION:The 2008 Mumbai attacks\, colloquially known as 26/11\, were a 
 coordinated series of twelve Islamic terrorist attacks carried out in Mumb
 ai\, Maharashtra\, India\, from 26 to 29 November 2008\, by ten members of
  the Lashkar-e-Taiba. A total of 175 people died\, including 166 civilians
  and nine of the attackers\, and more than 300 people were injured.\n\nCri
 sis: India\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Mumbai_attacks\nTex
 t: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
