DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20090406
SUMMARY:2009 Macedonian presidential election (North Macedonia)
DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Macedonia in 2009. The firs
 t round was held on 22 March\, alongside local elections. As no candidate 
 received more than 50% of the vote\, a run-off round was held on 5 April 2
 009\, which was won by Gjorge Ivanov of the center-right VMRO-DPMNE party.
  Incumbent President Branko Crvenkovski did not stand for re-election.\n\n
 Election: North Macedonia\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_Mace
 donian_presidential_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jd
