SUMMARY:Earthquake: 2009 L'Aquila earthquake (Italy)
DESCRIPTION:An earthquake occurred in the region of Abruzzo\, in southern I
 taly\, at 03:32 CEST on 6 April 2009. It measured 6.3 on the moment magnit
 ude scale and 5.8 or 5.9 on the Richter scale\; its epicentre was near L'A
 quila\, the capital of Abruzzo\, which together with surrounding villages 
 suffered the most damage.\n\nCrisis: Italy\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.o
 rg/wiki/2009_L%27Aquila_earthquake\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via P
 RP (jdpi.pages.dev).
