SUMMARY:Terrorist attack: 2009 Nevsky Express bombing (Russia)
DESCRIPTION:The 2009 Nevsky Express bombing occurred on 27 November 2009 wh
 en a bomb exploded under a high speed train travelling between the Russian
  cities of Moscow and Saint Petersburg causing derailment near the town of
  Bologoye\, Tver Oblast\, on the Moscow–Saint Petersburg Railway. The de
 railment occurred at 21:34 local time.\n\nCrisis: Russia\nSource: https://
 en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_Nevsky_Express_bombing\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-
 SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
